cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Aerostore or its benchmark and verification methodology in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Aerostore: a shared-memory transactional database engine in Rust"
abstract: >-
  Aerostore is an experimental Rust database engine for high-ingest,
  frequently updated state shared between processes on one host. It combines
  process-shared storage, serializable optimistic transactions with
  transactional secondary indexes, and write-ahead logging. The engine was
  built with AI coding agents and is checked by component proofs (Verus and
  Lean), TLA+ and Loom models, reference-model oracles, and benchmark sandboxes
  that retain failed and inconclusive results.
authors:
  - given-names: Zach
    family-names: Conn
repository-code: "https://github.com/zpconn/aerostore"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - database
  - storage engine
  - shared memory
  - MVCC
  - optimistic concurrency control
  - formal verification
  - Verus
  - Lean
  - TLA+
  - AI-assisted software engineering
